 "notes": [
  "Primary line: the per-shower mean of each shower's fraction of its own energy per bin (N = 287 showers); every shower weighs the same. Dashed line: the pooled ratio of sums, Σ energy in the bin over Σ shower energy, the notebook's estimator; it weights each shower by its energy, so high-momentum showers dominate it.",
  "Shaded band: the sample SD of the per-shower fractions (ddof = 1), where individual showers lie. Capped envelope: the 95% Student-t interval of the mean, each shower its own sampling unit. The pooled line's capped interval is the linearised ratio interval with events as clusters.",
  "Each shower is normalised by its own deposited energy, every hit kept (including those behind its entry plane), so its fractions sum to one over the bins of each axis; energy outside the drawn window stays in the normaliser, so the curves integrate to less than 100%.",
  "The notebook point-bins hit centres in 20 mm depth bins over 0–1200 mm and 10 mm radial bins over 0–500 mm, pooled over the whole file. Here each hit is footprint-splatted into 6 × 6 × 2 sub-deposits rotated by its shower's R(θ, φ), depth is binned at the layer pitch (20.5 mm) anchored at w = 0, and the pooled line sums this selection only.",
  "ρ = √(u² + v²) is each sub-deposit's 2-D distance from its shower's incident axis; values are per cm of radius with no 2πρ area factor, as in the notebook. The 10 mm radial bins are finer than one cell (48.27 × 48.60 mm), so part of the SD band is cell discretisation, not shower-to-shower variation. Beyond ρ = 50 cm lies 14.13% of the pooled energy (overflow), kept in the normaliser.",
  "Native depth: each shower's own sampling layers counted from its first, Δz = kt × 20.5 mm in the per-shower translated frame. It is not rotated, so it is not w; one bin per layer, never splatted, so no binning comb can arise there (layer-to-layer lag-1 −0.09, recorded, not a comb verdict).",
  "Footprint splat k = 6 transverse, k_z = 2 in depth. Projected sub-deposit spacing 8.1 mm against the 10 mm ρ bin: gap-free in one dimension, which a 1-D profile needs (a 2-D raster at this bin would need k = 7). Comb lag-1 of this selection's raw pooled profile, every bin before the display window: ρ +0.78 (combed below −0.10); no comb.",
  "1 of the 287 showers deposits in one cell: its profile is that cell's splat footprint alone, which widens the SD band.",
  "The y range follows the two lines only; band and interval parts beyond it are clipped at the axis with an out-of-range marker, and tooltips carry the true values. kt: 1 SD-band bin(s) above the range, 1 envelope bin(s) above the range, 25 SD-band bin(s) below zero; ρ: 2 SD-band bin(s) above the range, 2 envelope bin(s) above the range, 45 SD-band bin(s) below zero."
